Original paths that are not reproduced
--------------------------------------
09:EC2A ObjectSlideGateUpStep, a hit with the fog colour at $7FFF: the
original runs operand bytes as code and ends in ROM data at $CA:E7EC. Here
the frame ends. Direct page $5C and $0DA7 are written by these objects and
read by nothing, so those writes are left out; $1A05 likewise (only the
unreached SlideOutWobble reads it).
Work RAM $0000 is the race step's flag (g.frame_stage_00, 2 while a step
runs): the rails' first colour and the shards' third axis read it. The
burst gate's pitch reads direct page $80 (course 2 has the only burst gate):
taken as 0. In the all-courses play (27,500 frames traced) only the
power-on clear wrote $7F or $80, and no label in the code names $80; the
play never drives far enough to set up the burst gate, so its own read was
not seen.
A link of 0 (a race's first step, before the cars are linked) leads the
original to read a camera record at work RAM $0000. Traced in race1: its
mode is the step flag, its object ObjectPlaceAll's count (0), its X
ObjectPlaceAll's starter number, its Y the last worked Y, the rest only the
power-on clear; the view routine then reads the object again after its own
rescaling left the rescaled X there. camera_at_link() gives that record;
the native first step's view position and origins equal the recording's
((5, $F2CE, 0), ($420, $20, $400) twice).
Course entries with flag bit 9 and no model record (+$20 = 0), 35 to 67
per course, add work RAM $000A/$000C/$000E to their offsets. Traced in the
original (sfxbox access log) before each course load of the four
recordings: $000A was last written by ObjectPlaceOnParent (its doubled
turned Y offset; attract demo 2, $FFD2) or ObjectFaceTied (the camera's Y;
race1 $F2CE, battle $E64E), and not at all since power-on in attract demo 1
(0); $000C-$000F only by the power-on clear. Kept as g.last_worked_y,
written at both places. Checked natively: both attract loads match the
recording object for object (88 and 119 objects, models and offsets).
race1 and battle are not checked natively: the game cannot yet be driven
through the menus to those races. Other routines also write $000A
(RotateXY, RotateXZFrom08, ObjectMoveForward's and ObjectTrailSign's sign
stores, ObjectPieceSpray's) but none was the last writer before a course
load in the four recordings; they do not update the field.
Stray stores to low RAM on paths that need a missing record or an empty
list are skipped, with a comment where each is: ring_spawn, the track
director with no entry, ObjectFree with no next, the sky ball when the spawn
fails, ObjectPlaceAll and GsuRecordWords88 with a count of 0.

The earlier remaster's Enhanced calls: what became of each (2026-11-09)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
The game runs a whole step every 6 updates (4 on the course menu) and draws
the 3D between steps from places and angles set between the last two
steps' ends (fx/fx_tween.c: the cameras' places and angles, the objects'
places and angles, the Super FX records' places and angles, a car's parts'
places). With whole steps the remaster's sharing calls (rm_share,
rm_share_by, rm_sharing, rm_eased8/16, rm_step_due) gave the step's change
unchanged, so the code without them is the remaster's whole-step game.
Each such site changes either a place or an angle, which the pictures
between set, or a frame, colour, count or timer, which steps once a step in
the original and in the remaster's whole steps alike: a picture's or a
colour's number has no value between two.

Covered: places and angles, set between by fx_tween
- car_parts.c rm_eased16, rm_eased8, return_frame (PartDetachStep, a part
  going back): its place and angles.
- object.c apply_velocity (rm_share): its place.
- object_handlers.c rm_eased16, rm_eased8, ObjectChildReturn: a child's
  place and angles.
- object_handlers.c CameraApproachTarget (rm_eased16, rm_share): the
  camera's place offsets, which the step makes the camera's place; its
  count is below.
- objects_09.c add8s, add16s, add16_vias, ease8s: places (+$0C-$10) and
  angles (+$14-$16); where they change +$27, +$29 (a bob's offset and
  speed, a ball's target), +$48, +$49 or +$0A, those are counts and timers.
- objects_09.c rail_slide, GateSlideStep, ObjectShardStep,
  ObjectFloaterStep, swing_frame: places and angles (the floater's and the
  swing's +$0A are timers).
- orient.c ease_half, ObjectFaceTied; replay_camera.c zoom_frame: the
  camera's angles.

Covered: once a step, as in the original
- object.c ObjectsRunHandlers (rm_share): the run count +$36 and the
  objects' frame count (the frames chosen by it).
- object_handlers.c count_down, CameraDirectorWait, CameraApproachTarget's
  count: counts.
- object_handlers.c ObjectBlinkerFade: a colour step and the record flag.
- object_handlers.c ObjectPieceFall: its frame (the sprite turn) and life;
  its place is set between.
- object_handlers.c PlayerCarEvents: sounds and the records' events.
- object_handlers.c ObjectLampDrop: a startled eye's spin (+$48) and size
  (+$5F), a step at a time as the remaster had them; its place on the car
  is set between, its gaze goes between (ObjectGazeBetween, below).
- objects_09.c counter_tick, dec8s, inc8s, colour_cycle, colour_cycle6,
  rail_drop_frame, bounce_colour: counts, frames and colours (the bounce's
  offset moves a marker's height, which is set between).
- objects_09.c bob_frame: only ObjectBob (dead) and its step, reached from
  it alone, use it.

Done in object/animate.c (the remaster's animate.c) and draw_list.c
- object.c ObjectInit (rm_object_made): ObjectMade.
- object.c ObjectsRunHandlers (rm_object_turn): ObjectTurn: whether it
  ran; the lap balls', bumpers' and bonus markers' looks go on while they
  do not run.
- object.c ObjectGroupsActivate (rm_objects_keep_running):
  ObjectsKeepRunning: the dolphins, rings, spinners and their centres, the
  swing, the floater and the pop marker run wherever they are.
- objects_09.c fan_frame (rm_object_kept): ObjectKept: no sound from one
  kept running.
- draw_list.c far_records (rm_far_left_out): ObjectFarLeftOut: not drawn
  far before its set-up has run (unless its look is known) or while a short
  life is stopped.
- draw_list.c draw_record (rm_record_look): ObjectRecordLook: a set-up's
  known look, far; the looks that go on. The angles' fractions between
  steps are fx_tween's own (records_take_fractions).
- draw_list.c far_record (rm_look_dy): ObjectLookDy.
- draw_list.c parked_child (rm_enhanced, rm_redrawing): parked_child: a
  parked car's tyres drawn on it, far.
- draw_list.c ObjectDrawListBuild (rm_enhanced, rm_whole_steps): the far
  records (56ea23c6), in every 3D scene.
- object.c ObjectNearFocus (rm_enhanced): a car stays near, a model, however
  far.
- draw_list.c draw_record (rm_gaze_of): object_gaze and draw_record_gaze;
  between steps the gaze goes from the last step's to this one's
  (ObjectGazeBetween).

With the 3D session's 306606ed and 011ff881
- The looks and gazes between steps go by fx_tween_t (how far through its
  step a picture is).
- A parked tyre of a car in the near list is marked (FX_FAR_PARKED) and
  drawn among the near objects by depth.
- Circling pieces keep to their circle between steps: fx_tween adds
  ObjectOrbitBetween's offset after the straight-line place.
